WEBVTT

00:01.694 --> 00:03.794
I wonder if she's gotten out
of the rain somewhere.

00:05.304 --> 00:07.204
I have to hurry up and find her.

00:09.404 --> 00:10.874
Amino...

00:12.104 --> 00:16.774
Amino, I'm sure you'll be able to find her.

00:20.284 --> 00:24.154
Thank you... Miss Sato.

00:30.094 --> 00:31.584
Amino...

00:33.364 --> 00:34.764
My...

00:36.594 --> 00:38.624
My name is...

00:41.234 --> 00:44.434
Something reached for but cannot be grasped...

00:45.874 --> 00:49.404
Something that strays from that hand,
going far away...

00:51.044 --> 00:55.384
People will always pursue such things.

00:56.414 --> 00:59.784
And before long, become lost.

01:05.864 --> 01:10.324
This is our story of one such summer.

01:28.654 --> 01:30.084
Living for the Day
After Tomorrow

01:30.084 --> 01:33.754
Living for the Day
After Tomorrow
The children's graffiti

01:33.754 --> 01:34.224
Living for the Day
After Tomorrow

01:34.524 --> 01:38.184
That has blossomed on the asphalt

01:38.964 --> 01:42.594
Shimmers in the waves of heat

01:43.434 --> 01:46.264
And has begun to walk

01:46.404 --> 01:51.244
At that promised hill

01:51.244 --> 01:54.874
That no one knows

01:55.414 --> 02:00.114
Encounter the miraculous time called "today"

02:00.114 --> 02:04.884
That comes only once - feel it

02:04.884 --> 02:09.054
Chase the flowing clouds

02:09.054 --> 02:13.394
Even now, they seem in your grasp

02:13.394 --> 02:17.764
A premonition, heart beating with excitement

02:17.764 --> 02:22.394
A destiny that has begun to move

02:22.504 --> 02:26.874
So bright that you awaken

02:26.874 --> 02:30.904
Hotter even than the morning sun

02:31.144 --> 02:35.044
Sparkling without end

02:35.384 --> 02:42.684
Embraced in the season of light

02:58.644 --> 03:00.664
I always wanted to bring you here one day.

03:07.354 --> 03:08.784
Yes!

03:13.654 --> 03:16.784
Thank you very much, Amino.

03:20.094 --> 03:21.924
Iokawa...

03:33.274 --> 03:34.574
Miss Sato?

03:37.714 --> 03:39.474
Good morning!

03:39.884 --> 03:41.684
How are you feeling?

03:46.784 --> 03:50.914
The Present That Exists There

03:54.664 --> 03:56.134
Here you are.

03:57.764 --> 03:59.094
Thank you for the food.

04:05.844 --> 04:06.934
This is great!

04:07.174 --> 04:09.144
Miss Sato made it.

04:09.144 --> 04:10.734
She did?

04:10.914 --> 04:12.974
Yes. Now eat up.

04:13.854 --> 04:17.214
Um, may I borrow your bicycle again later?

04:17.724 --> 04:19.724
You plan on going out?

04:19.724 --> 04:23.224
I'm all better now! The weather's cleared up, too.

04:23.224 --> 04:24.554
Um, I...

04:25.324 --> 04:28.664
I think you should rest. Also...

04:31.464 --> 04:34.304
It's important to give yourself time to recover.

04:34.304 --> 04:37.134
You need to rest a little longer.

04:37.404 --> 04:38.434
Yes, ma'am.

04:51.184 --> 04:54.554
37.1 degrees Celsius. You're almost there.

04:55.424 --> 04:57.894
It's important to let yourself get better.

05:00.164 --> 05:02.524
Will you go looking again?

05:05.504 --> 05:09.664
Once you're better, will you go looking
for Miss lokawa again?

05:10.204 --> 05:11.074
Yeah.

05:12.944 --> 05:14.344
I had a dream.

05:16.544 --> 05:19.314
I took lokawa to the river's source.

05:21.554 --> 05:25.044
We looked at the water together...
Looked at the scenery...

05:26.554 --> 05:28.644
And then all of a sudden...

05:35.164 --> 05:36.794
No, never mind.

05:47.174 --> 05:48.834
Do you mind?

05:49.144 --> 05:52.304
This last one. I'm going to eat it.

05:53.714 --> 05:54.544
Go ahead.

05:56.554 --> 05:58.414
Any word from Tetsu?

05:59.554 --> 06:01.524
Oh! Thaf foy, he mehvr...

06:01.524 --> 06:02.954
You can finish eating first.

06:08.534 --> 06:12.694
That boy, he never gets in touch
unless something big has happened.

06:13.604 --> 06:16.904
"No news is good news,"
I guess you could say, huh?

06:17.874 --> 06:19.544
You're not worried?

06:19.544 --> 06:23.274
Well, so long as he ends up
finding Karada, then...

06:24.184 --> 06:25.904
I'm so sorry.

06:26.484 --> 06:28.054
Don't worry about it.

06:28.054 --> 06:30.884
The truth is, I'm really not that worried.

06:33.384 --> 06:36.514
He may be an idiot, but in his own idiotic way...

06:37.494 --> 06:39.514
Or maybe it's BECAUSE he's an idiot...

06:39.994 --> 06:44.994
He has an inner strength.
He's courageous and straightforward.

06:47.234 --> 06:48.964
The exact opposite of me, huh?

06:55.944 --> 06:58.774
That's not true at all, don't you think?

07:21.274 --> 07:22.474
What?

07:22.474 --> 07:26.404
Well, this is our first time.
The two of us alone on a trip...

07:26.404 --> 07:29.534
But why visit the highlands?

07:29.944 --> 07:31.974
There are some flowers I want to see.

07:44.824 --> 07:46.084
Here.

08:02.144 --> 08:03.374
What do you think?

08:03.714 --> 08:04.984
It's hard to say...

08:04.984 --> 08:06.984
Actually, they're kinda plain.

08:06.984 --> 08:08.844
That's their appeal.

08:42.714 --> 08:45.314
Big Brother! Wait!

08:45.984 --> 08:48.284
Hurry up! I'll leave ya here!

08:48.394 --> 08:50.084
Wait!

09:04.444 --> 09:09.674
I wanted to hurry up and be an adult
so I could let Hiro be free, right now.

09:10.944 --> 09:14.674
She wanted them to make her an adult.

09:14.854 --> 09:21.784
And like some kind of trade-off, even though
I didn't wish for anything, I became a child...

09:26.024 --> 09:28.964
Maybe I, too...

09:31.304 --> 09:32.524
We're back!

09:33.004 --> 09:35.594
Hello there. How did it go?

09:39.974 --> 09:42.844
Wow! What a big haul!

09:43.444 --> 09:46.434
It won't be hard to fix up tonight's menu!

09:46.684 --> 09:48.614
Thanks, Darling.

09:49.954 --> 09:52.384
We bought them at a fish store!

09:52.384 --> 09:53.544
I know.

09:58.764 --> 10:01.994
Huh? Tetsu, should you be up already?

10:02.234 --> 10:03.594
I'm totally fine.

10:04.034 --> 10:06.004
No use just lying around all day.

10:06.004 --> 10:08.734
Ah, that's good news.

10:08.734 --> 10:11.074
Hey, you wanna go for a walk?

10:11.244 --> 10:15.044
Breathing some outside air
will probably do you some good.

10:15.044 --> 10:16.404
Yeah, you're right!

10:18.914 --> 10:21.754
The food will be ready soon,
so be sure to hurry back.

10:21.754 --> 10:22.954
Score!

10:22.954 --> 10:25.144
Kotomi, you'll be helping me with dinner.

10:26.454 --> 10:29.724
I can't prep all this fish on my own!

10:29.724 --> 10:30.694
What?

10:31.764 --> 10:33.024
All right, Miss Sato.

10:33.024 --> 10:33.994
What?

10:34.464 --> 10:35.434
If you'd be so kind.

10:35.434 --> 10:37.494
Uh, yes ma'am.

10:47.474 --> 10:52.744
Um, so, thank you. For everything.

10:53.284 --> 10:54.684
Not at all.

10:54.684 --> 10:57.844
But really, I'm better now, so...

10:58.224 --> 10:59.414
Okay.

11:00.594 --> 11:02.024
That...

11:03.964 --> 11:07.194
That dream from last night. How did it turn out?

11:07.534 --> 11:10.624
Oh. It was no big deal.

11:11.064 --> 11:15.364
You came here, didn't you? With Miss lokawa.

11:16.104 --> 11:17.434
Yeah.

11:17.804 --> 11:22.104
It was Miss lokawa's brother, your sister...

11:22.974 --> 11:26.144
Hiro's friend Shoko...

11:27.854 --> 11:29.514
And me.

11:31.024 --> 11:35.824
I'm Karada lokawa.

11:52.674 --> 11:54.974
Miss Sato? Um...

11:56.014 --> 11:58.074
I'll do this.

11:58.544 --> 12:00.854
You've done enough, so just rest.

12:00.854 --> 12:02.044
I'm fine.

12:02.514 --> 12:05.424
R-really? Well then, if you don't mind.

12:05.424 --> 12:06.414
Ma'am.

12:12.724 --> 12:16.524
I wonder what happened between
Miss Sato and Amino.

12:16.934 --> 12:19.494
They've been acting strange ever
since they came back.

12:19.904 --> 12:22.264
Somehow, it doesn't feel like the time to ask.

12:22.934 --> 12:25.934
Even Amino just went straight up to his room.

12:26.544 --> 12:28.204
I'll go ask!

12:29.544 --> 12:30.634
H-hey!

12:36.514 --> 12:38.384
Wishing stones?!

12:43.224 --> 12:47.094
By "wishing stones," you mean those things
under the camphor tree?

12:48.294 --> 12:52.664
So Miss Sato is the girl you've been looking for?

12:53.004 --> 12:55.264
Who could believe something like that?

12:56.274 --> 12:59.574
I have no idea why she'd say that to me.

13:06.544 --> 13:07.584
How are things?

13:07.584 --> 13:11.414
Well, they're... Where's Miss Sato?

13:12.054 --> 13:15.924
She went outside once she'd finished the dishes.
She's probably at the cape.

13:18.594 --> 13:20.264
What's with you?

13:20.264 --> 13:21.924
Ah, well...

13:22.334 --> 13:27.964
It looks like she told Amino
something of an interesting tale.

13:28.604 --> 13:32.244
"Interesting"? Like the kind you always tell?

13:32.244 --> 13:36.334
Apparently, Amino didn't take too kindly to it.

13:36.614 --> 13:38.484
Yes, but still...

13:38.484 --> 13:41.504
For Amino to get so angry
over something like that...

13:44.884 --> 13:51.094
Thirty minutes into our first date,
you got angry and went back home.

13:51.094 --> 13:54.994
Well, if someone suddenly starts talking
about goblins and monsters...

13:54.994 --> 13:57.934
Yet here you are now.

13:59.304 --> 14:01.574
Even if a person gets angry at first,

14:01.574 --> 14:06.564
sooner or later that thing called romance
will fill him with warmth.

14:07.274 --> 14:09.934
In any case, let's keep a friendly eye on them.

14:30.234 --> 14:32.224
Ah, there you are!

14:35.534 --> 14:40.374
So this is where you like to hang out, is it?

14:40.644 --> 14:41.664
Um...

14:44.544 --> 14:47.174
I heard all about it from Tetsu.

14:48.614 --> 14:50.944
About the wishing stones.

14:53.784 --> 14:57.224
That story even surprised Mr. Isogai!

14:57.224 --> 15:01.894
Because of some rocks, you became an adult
and your friend turned into a kid...

15:02.334 --> 15:08.164
It's interesting enough, but I don't think
it's too funny for Tetsu right now.

15:08.434 --> 15:10.164
It's the truth.

15:16.574 --> 15:18.414
Were you born in Kanocho?

15:18.414 --> 15:19.314
What?

15:19.314 --> 15:22.144
Where were you born? Kanocho?

15:24.184 --> 15:30.454
It's my hometown. So I know
all about the wishing stones.

15:30.454 --> 15:35.484
Ever since I was little, my dad would tell me
about them during our walks.

15:35.664 --> 15:38.264
"These rocks make wishes come true."

15:38.264 --> 15:41.294
"They're sure to make yours come true, too."

15:41.704 --> 15:47.474
Even though they never granted any of
HIS wishes, he'd always go on about it.

15:48.214 --> 15:53.484
My mom was always like,
"Stop teaching that girl such silly things!"

15:53.484 --> 15:55.954
She'd get so angry, it was such a mess...

15:56.314 --> 15:58.654
He sounds like Mr. Isogai.

15:58.954 --> 16:01.084
Yeah, I guess he does.

16:03.094 --> 16:04.384
But...

16:05.924 --> 16:10.264
But if your story really is true...

16:11.304 --> 16:12.404
I...

16:12.404 --> 16:14.134
It is true!

16:16.574 --> 16:19.404
I... I really am...

16:19.404 --> 16:21.564
Karada lokawa!

16:26.444 --> 16:29.984
Do you remember when we came to this beach?

16:29.984 --> 16:36.654
I said that Shoko and I wished on the wishing
stones but what I'd wished for was a secret.

16:37.724 --> 16:40.194
I wished to become an adult.

16:41.194 --> 16:43.594
To become one right away.

16:44.364 --> 16:47.964
The stones made that wish come true.

16:49.034 --> 16:55.064
I'm sorry for not telling you until now.
I didn't think you'd believe me.

16:57.414 --> 16:59.274
But I was happy.

16:59.944 --> 17:03.884
You've looked for me this whole time...

17:03.884 --> 17:04.944
And you found me.

17:05.854 --> 17:07.484
What the hell's your problem?

17:08.894 --> 17:10.654
What are you talking about?

17:11.394 --> 17:13.664
Why would you tell me something like that?

17:13.664 --> 17:15.324
Amino...

17:15.864 --> 17:18.734
What is this? Some kind of joke?

17:19.404 --> 17:21.304
You're making fun of me?

17:21.304 --> 17:24.874
N-no! I'm not making fun of you at all!

17:24.874 --> 17:28.214
I really am Karada! I'm Karada lokawa!

17:28.214 --> 17:29.504
Cut the crap!

17:30.714 --> 17:34.854
You think I won't find her, don't you?!
That's why you're saying this!

17:34.854 --> 17:37.684
No, that's not it! I really am!

17:37.684 --> 17:40.954
I'll find her. I WILL find lokawa!

17:41.124 --> 17:44.094
Wait, Amino! I'm Karada!

17:44.094 --> 17:48.064
Karada lokawa, the girl you tried to take
to see that river but couldn't!

17:48.064 --> 17:50.934
Here, on this beach, we played volleyball!

17:51.264 --> 17:57.404
You made fun of my floatie.
But you comforted me when I cried!

17:57.404 --> 18:00.104
Then you forgot that the next day we had school!

18:02.144 --> 18:04.514
Amino...

18:13.684 --> 18:18.754
Please believe me. I... I...

18:43.714 --> 18:44.914
Hiro
lokawa

18:54.564 --> 18:55.754
Yes?

18:57.434 --> 18:59.694
What is it, Karada?

19:01.304 --> 19:06.504
Miss Shoko, I... I don't know what to do.

19:06.504 --> 19:08.164
Did something happen?

19:10.044 --> 19:13.704
Amino hates me.

19:14.784 --> 19:16.714
Are you with him?

19:17.214 --> 19:21.744
He didn't believe me. That I... I'm me.

19:23.554 --> 19:25.084
You told him.

19:25.924 --> 19:32.734
I told him how we played volleyball here
and how he made fun of my floatie...

19:33.564 --> 19:36.904
But I guess there's reason he'd believe me, huh?

19:37.534 --> 19:42.494
But I thought for sure he'd understand.
Because Amino...

19:45.384 --> 19:51.254
I... when I'm with him,
I feel relieved somehow, and warm.

19:53.024 --> 19:54.384
That's why...

19:55.054 --> 19:57.824
Karada... Are you?

20:02.094 --> 20:04.084
Hello?! Karada!

20:06.304 --> 20:07.794
Oh...

20:11.504 --> 20:12.774
Hello?

20:12.774 --> 20:14.034
What?

20:15.944 --> 20:17.744
It's just like you said.

20:18.414 --> 20:19.384
What is?

20:20.344 --> 20:22.974
I... I've been a coward.

20:23.554 --> 20:25.124
Yeah, you have.

20:25.124 --> 20:27.554
A spineless coward.

20:28.654 --> 20:32.114
Is it cowardly to have this kind of
conversation over the phone?

20:32.994 --> 20:35.654
It beats doing it by air mail. Keep going.

20:36.594 --> 20:42.334
It's true, I've just run away from things.
From you, from Karada...

20:43.034 --> 20:48.274
By breaking up with you in a letter,
by saying nothing to Karada...

20:49.744 --> 20:52.344
Because rather than telling the truth,

20:52.344 --> 20:58.184
it was easier to be hated by you
and to be Karada's "real" brother.

21:01.294 --> 21:05.694
I'm the one who took away
her place to call home.

21:06.764 --> 21:09.334
I'm going to go looking for her.

21:09.334 --> 21:12.934
I don't know where she is, but I will find...

21:12.934 --> 21:13.164
I know where she is.
I don't know where she is, but I will find...

21:13.164 --> 21:14.964
I know where she is.

21:16.304 --> 21:19.904
She's at the beach.
The one we went to together.

21:26.714 --> 21:29.144
Yes. That's right. Thanks.

21:30.054 --> 21:33.884
Please let me have the day off today.
I'm sorry for the bother. Yes.

21:34.384 --> 21:38.384
A new present, a now that can be reached
if you stretch out your hand...

21:39.464 --> 21:42.324
That's what she's trying to grab hold of.

21:43.334 --> 21:46.794
Yet her hand stops, trembling,
just before she reaches it.

21:47.864 --> 21:49.634
In which case, I...

21:50.034 --> 21:51.404
We...

21:59.184 --> 22:01.044
Shall we go?

22:02.154 --> 22:03.414
Yeah.

22:14.494 --> 22:20.734
Wearing unfamiliar shoes

22:20.734 --> 22:25.464
Each step a pain that I endure

22:26.904 --> 22:33.184
And yet I walk

22:33.184 --> 22:37.984
Because I have a place to return to

22:38.754 --> 22:46.894
I stare at myself

22:46.894 --> 22:51.494
And notice something I'd lost

22:54.634 --> 23:00.804
I want to be with you

23:00.804 --> 23:07.514
To feel it, near and far

23:07.514 --> 23:13.384
To keep creating each normal day

23:13.384 --> 23:20.024
With you, my beloved

23:20.024 --> 23:27.454
To say "I'm home,"
remove my shoes and hold you

23:27.704 --> 23:32.534
My sweet home

23:45.254 --> 23:46.914
Summer will come to an end.

23:47.084 --> 23:49.054
The seasons will change.

23:49.194 --> 23:52.214
A single stretch of road, continuing ever onward.

23:52.424 --> 23:54.914
Unable to see behind or forward.

23:55.534 --> 23:56.964
Hold hands...

23:57.094 --> 23:58.894
Don't let go...

23:59.134 --> 24:01.194
The one who is by my side is...

24:01.474 --> 24:02.904
You.

24:03.504 --> 24:06.304
On the last episode of
Living for the Day After Tomorrow:

24:06.304 --> 24:07.204
"To Be Here"

24:07.204 --> 24:07.944
Final episode
To Be Here
"To Be Here"

24:07.944 --> 24:12.744
Final episode
To Be Here
